ent":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consider degrading a `resolve_ref` failure in the post-close drift guard to a closed-without-signature warning (like the SigningError path) rather than letting it raise after the close committed.","criteria":["error-handling"],"decision":"dropped","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:669: '_fresh_sha = resolve_ref(ref, str(config.repo_root(repo_root)), fetch=False)' (no try/except around it)","src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:376-382: 'raise SnapshotRefError(...)' when the ref does not resolve","src/rebar/signing.py:511-525: the HEAD branch's `head_sha` returns 'unknown' rather than raising, so the two branches differ in failure mode","transition_close.py:678-691: the else-branch handles signing failures as warnings (close still succeeds, exit 0)"],"finding":"In the post-close drift guard, the `--ref` branch calls `resolve_ref(...)` which can raise `SnapshotRefError`; this is NOT wrapped in try/except and runs AFTER the ticket transition already committed, so a raise would surface as a hard failure — asymmetric with the surrounding block that deliberately degrades drift and signing failures to stderr warnings (exit 0).","id":"1","impact":0.32,"location":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:666-671","norm_id":"n4f70ea4011b6bfe6","priority":0.0914,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["The ref was resolvable at verify time but becomes unresolvable before the post-close sign (e.g. an object pruned / a branch deleted between verify and sign), raising after the close committed."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viabl