able surface"],"finding":"test_parse_flags_reads_ref asserts against the internal private helper `_transition._parse_flags` (membership in its return tuple) rather than observable CLI behavior, making it a change-detector that breaks on a behavior-preserving refactor (renaming/inlining `_parse_flags`) with no observable-behavior change.","id":"4","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_ref_target_80af.py:129","norm_id":"n48f7796bc839dc0b","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["A refactor inlines or renames `_parse_flags` into the transition dispatcher while preserving identical CLI flag-parsing behavior — the test breaks though nothing observable changed."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Assert `--ref <v>` and `--ref=<v>` behavior via `main([\"transition\", id, current, \"closed\", \"--ref\", sha])` and inspect the observable outcome (verifier call ref / signed result), rather than calling `_parse_flags` directly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":1,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"common","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a CLI end-to-end test that closes a story via `main(['transition', id, 'in_progress', 'closed', '--ref', sha])` and asserts the verifier received that ref and the close landed signed.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":"novelty-region","evidence":["test_close_ref_forwards_to_verifier_and_signs_at_target calls `rebar.transition(story, \"in_progress\", \"closed\", ref=sha1, ...)` (line 98) — library, not CLI","test_close_without_ref_targets_head calls `rebar.transition(story, \"in_progress\", \"closed\", ...)` (line 118) — library, not CLI","search_files for `--ref` in tests shows the transition-close CLI form is exercised nowhere; only `cli._verify_completion([... '--ref' ...])` and `_transition._parse_flags([...])` appear","The new CLI wiring is in src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:506 `reason, force, force_close, close_class, caused_by, ref = _parse_flags(flag_args)` and :516 `ref=(ref or None)` — untested via `main`"],"finding":"No test drives the `--ref` flag through the CLI entrypoint `main(['transition', id, current, 'closed', '--ref', sha])`; the two behavioral tests call the library `rebar.transition(ref=...)` directly and the third tests only the isolated parser, so the full CLI wiring (arg → _parse_flags → transition_compute → close_ticket → drift guard) is never exercised end-to-end.","id":"5","impact":0.248,"location":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_ref_target_80af.py","norm_id":"nbfc54c8f0ac773a7","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.2126,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["A regression that mis-threads `ref` between `_parse_flags` and `transition_compute` in the CLI dispatch (e.g. wrong tuple po